# §43: vendored sample library — gigabytes, rebuilt with npm run sounds:vendor
# public/samples/ is COMMITTED since §202. It is 24 MB of Vorbis, and it has to
# be in the repository or a deploy built from GitHub has no drums at all —
# `npm run sounds:vendor:used` fetches 296 MB from a third party, which is not
# something a build should depend on. Re-vendor it locally and compress it with
# scripts/compress-samples.mjs if it ever needs rebuilding.
# public/land/ is COMMITTED since the first deploy: it is the real Amsterdam
# terrain, and without it a deployed build quietly falls back to generated
# waves — a different world than the one that was tested. 20 MB, rebuildable
# with `npm run land:bake`.

# subagent worktrees: copies of this repo, never part of it
.claude/worktrees/
.playwright-mcp/
exports/
node-compile-cache/
